# What not to upload when deploying.
#
# Without this file the CLI uploaded the whole directory — 776 MB — and the
# deploy FAILED with "File size limit exceeded (100 MB)". The offenders were
# Turbopack's dev cache files under `.next/dev/cache`, individually 180–270 MB
# after a few days of `next dev`. Nothing here is needed anyway: Vercel installs
# dependencies and runs the build itself, from source.
#
# `data/` is deliberately NOT excluded. The app reads the player pool, the board
# and the keeper sheets out of `data/*.json` at runtime, so those files have to
# ship. They are about 9 MB.

# Build output and bundler caches. `.next-*` covers the alternate dist dirs the
# verification builds use via NEXT_DIST_DIR, which accumulate the same way.
.next
.next-*

# Vercel installs these itself.
node_modules

# Local verification artifacts.
screenshots
coverage

# Secrets live in the Vercel project's environment variables, which is where the
# deployment reads them from. Uploading a local copy would only risk drift.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Local scratch.
.DS_Store
*.log
